state:ChildGrowth a skos:Concept,
        ue:State ;
    skos:broader state:AnthropometricStatus ;
    skos:definition "Physical growth status and change in children, reflected in height or length, weight gain, head circumference, standardized anthropometric measures, or growth velocity." ;
    skos:inScheme state: ;
    skos:prefLabel "Child growth" ;
    skos:related indicator:BodyCompositionMeasurement,
        state:ChildHealthStatus,
        state:InfantHealthStatus,
        state:Stunting,
        state:Wasting ;
    skos:scopeNote "Use for generic continuous or non-threshold physical growth status or change in children, including height or length, weight gain, head circumference, standardized anthropometric measures, or growth velocity. Use Stunting when an explicit stunting diagnosis or height-for-age or length-for-age below -2 standard deviations is established; use Wasting when explicit wasting or qualifying weight-for-height or mid-upper arm circumference evidence is established; and use SevereAcuteMalnutrition when SAM, severe anthropometric thresholds, or nutritional oedema is explicit. One source record may map directly to ChildGrowth and one or more condition concepts when independent evidence supports each mapping; this evidence-level multi-mapping does not create taxonomy polyhierarchy." ;
    ue:bearer <https://universalevidence.com/vocab/subjects/Population> .

